otal":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":265496132631976,"name":"RYM Top — Hip Hop — Gangstarap","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":23,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":3080531282495,"name":"AOTY Must Hear 1970s","src":"musthear","grp":null,"list_year":null,"rank":67,"year":null,"note":null,"total":256,"scaruffi":null}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"In March 1977, Pink Floyd embarked on a tour for their *Animals* record, including a series of five shows at Wembley Stadium in London. The concerts featured the band's staple large inflatable pig. Critics like Ed Jones in *The Spectator* viewed these spectacles critically, suggesting the band cultivated anonymity on stage, acting as \"little more than backing musicians providing mood music for their own gimmicks of presentation.\" By 1977, Pink Floyd was widely considered a \"legit supergroup.\" \"He's about a series of five shows that Pink Floyd did at Wembley Stadium in London on their tour for their animals record. He was referring to the large inflatable pig that was a staple at the show.\"","year":1977,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 42 - Rock Operas of the 70s","url":"https://seventies.libsyn.com/ep-42-rock-operas-of-the-70s"},{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 42 - Rock Operas of the 70s","url":null}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"The iconic album cover for \"Animals\" was designed by Storm Thorgerson, whose distinctive visual style greatly contributed to the band's aesthetic. His creation for this album is recognized among his most impactful works. \"So yeah, Dark Side of the Moon, wish you were here in animals, all are his creations.\"","year":1977,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The Stories Behind Iconic Album Covers Part 2","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_tbKuJR0cPs"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"There exists a lost guitar solo performed by Snowy White that appears exclusively on the 8-track edition of *Animals* (1977) and has never been commercially reissued in any other format. \"A lost guitar solo by Snowy White exists only on the 8-track edition of the album and was never commercially reissued.\"","year":1977,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"60 Mind-Blowing Facts About Music in 60 Minutes: The 2023 Edition","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qtdetc5-MQo"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Lost Guitar Solo by Snowy White Found Only on 8-Track Edition","body":"There exists a lost guitar solo performed by Snowy White that appears exclusively on the 8-track edition of *Animals* (1977) and has never been commercially reissued in any other format. \"A lost guitar solo by Snowy White exists only on the 8-track edition of the album and was never commercially reissued.\"","year":1977,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"60 Mind-Blowing Facts About Music in 60 Minutes: The 2023 Edition","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qtdetc5-MQo"}]}],"book_tracks":[{"id":242242618103336,"artist":"Pink Floyd","artist_id":154607196593337,"title":"Animals","year":1977,"ess":0,"yt":"D4KQae9oMWs","kind":null,"book":{"id":5,"title":"Heavy Metal: The Music and Its Culture","author":"Deena Weinstein","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/HeavyMetal/"},"scene":"Psicodelia y acid rock","scene_id":82200059192729,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/HeavyMetal/#psicodelia-acid-rock","chapters":["Cap. 2: Heavy metal: la bestia que se niega a morir"],"pages":[[1,27],[1,282]]}],"others":[{"id":281150642851607,"type":"album","name":"The Dark Side of the Moon","year":1973,"weight":139},{"id":273393047641424,"type":"album","name":"Wish You Were Here","year":1975,"weight":78},{"id":162610531324131,"type":"album","name":"The Wall","year":1979,"weight":76},{"id":249172959515508,"type":"album","name":"Meddle","year":1971,"weight